      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Verso (second section)",
          "value": "\n<ol><li>\n<p>that were found in the hands of Yeshu, your disciple&mdash; if</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>you tell us the truth, we will release you, but if not,</p>\n</li>\n<li>you and Yeshu will be executed by a double-edged sword.&rdquo;</li>\n<li>\n<p>Yoh\u0323anan answered and said to them: &ldquo;Masters! These writings&mdash;</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Yeshu wrote them. I&mdash;Tiberinus Caesar had im[pris]oned me,</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>and Yeshu [...] did not show me,</p>\n</li>\n<li>but he and his eleven disciples wrote them</li>\n<li>\n<p>and were misleading people (with them).&rdquo; They answered</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>and said to him: &ldquo;The disciples of Yeshu&mdash;what are their names?&rdquo;</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>He said to them: &ldquo;Naqi and Matai and Luqa and Alqi</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>and Altigus and Yehudah, and Paulus and Patmus and Netzer</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>and Buni and Todah.&rdquo; [They ans]wered and said: &ldquo;Who is going</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>after them?&rdquo; Yehudah Svariota answered [... ...]</p>\n</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
